         VERSION=1.4
          SOURCE=kernel-FreeDOS-v$VERSION.tar.gz
     SOURCE_HASH=sha512:bdf4264499744a83cd1ef29c14b7e06e599f73518c5cdb6341c2eed5eb5cd36460bea531495bb5eefb33cbd8e8f1699d52f3460ccc48688f0432268c61e42414
         SOURCE2=freecom-FreeDOS-v$VERSION.tar.gz
    SOURCE2_HASH=sha512:e027b0a4d17f71305e56c155fa0e16c7fb8e2916d8b72049191fbfcd9284387422ae8b7007fb11b00f6f6bec285628b4077d2089f9c7d4a259d1b75b26275a29
SOURCE_DIRECTORY="$BUILD_DIRECTORY/$SPELL-$VERSION"
        WEB_SITE=https://www.freedos.org/
   SOURCE_URL[0]=https://gitlab.com/FreeDOS/base/kernel/-/archive/FreeDOS-v$VERSION/$SOURCE
  SOURCE2_URL[0]=https://gitlab.com/FreeDOS/base/freecom/-/archive/FreeDOS-v$VERSION/$SOURCE2
SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH=${SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH:-1742892048}
      LICENSE[0]=GPL-2.0-or-later
         ENTERED=20261003
        KEYWORDS="dos operating system"
           SHORT="free DOS-compatible operating system (lite image)"
cat << EOF
FreeDOS is a complete, free, DOS-compatible operating system meant for
classic PC hardware. It provides the kernel, the command interpreter, a
file system driver for FAT and a growing collection of DOS utilities.

This spell builds a minimal diskette image with only the kernel and
command interpreter, named x86boot-lite.img.

For the whole FreeDOS distribution use the freedos-bin spell, which installs
from the release media.
EOF
